fix-self-test-ecschnorr: compile AlgorithmTests.c without ECSCHNORR

Classification: build fix.

With ENABLE_SELF_TESTS = YES and ALG_ECSCHNORR = NO (profile-algorithms.patch),
TestEccSignAndVerify() does not compile: its ECSCHNORR case loads the
signature into TPMU_SIGNATURE's `ecschnorr` member, which only exists with
ALG_ECSCHNORR. The case is compiled only with ALG_ECSCHNORR, as in version 185
(an unimplemented algorithm never reaches TestAlgorithm()'s dispatch).

diff --git a/src/AlgorithmTests.c b/src/AlgorithmTests.c
--- a/src/AlgorithmTests.c
+++ b/src/AlgorithmTests.c
@@ -646,12 +646,14 @@ static TPM_RC TestEccSignAndVerify(TPM_ALG_ID scheme, ALGORITHM_VECTOR* toTest)
 	    LoadEccParameter(&testSig.signature.ecdsa.signatureR, &c_TestEcDsa_r);
 	    LoadEccParameter(&testSig.signature.ecdsa.signatureS, &c_TestEcDsa_s);
 	    break;
+#if ALG_ECSCHNORR
 	  case TPM_ALG_ECSCHNORR:
 	    LoadEccParameter(&testSig.signature.ecschnorr.signatureR,
 			     &c_TestEcSchnorr_r);
 	    LoadEccParameter(&testSig.signature.ecschnorr.signatureS,
 			     &c_TestEcSchnorr_s);
 	    break;
+#endif
 	  case TPM_ALG_SM2:
 	    // don't have a test for SM2
 	    return TPM_RC_SUCCESS;
